    {
      "section_id": "section-3",
      "parent_section_id": "section-2",
      "title": "Membrana celular",
      "level": 3,
      "order": 3,
      "heading_type": "numbered",
      "numbering": "1.1",
      "start_line": 7,
      "end_line": 9,
      "chunks": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "chunk-2",
          "parent_section_id": "section-3",
          "text": "La membrana celular regula el intercambio de sustancias. Esta formada por una bicapa lipidica y proteinas que participan en transporte, senalizacion y reconocimiento.",
          "order": 2,
          "start_line": 9,
          "end_line": 9,
          "word_count": 23,
          "character_count": 166,
          "chunk_type": "paragraph"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "section_id": "section-4",
      "parent_section_id": "section-2",
      "title": "Organelos",
      "level": 3,
      "order": 4,
      "heading_type": "numbered",
      "numbering": "1.2",
      "start_line": 11,
      "end_line": 13,
      "chunks": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "chunk-3",
          "parent_section_id": "section-4",
          "text": "Los organelos realizan tareas especificas. El nucleo guarda informacion genetica, las mitocondrias producen energia y los ribosomas participan en la sintesis de proteinas.",
          "order": 3,
          "start_line": 13,
          "end_line": 13,
          "word_count": 23,
          "character_count": 171,
          "chunk_type": "paragraph"
        }
      ]
